# SCENARIO: fix_170_cast_bot_channel   SEED: 0   CAMERAS: auto   BOTCFG: off
# Fix #170 - on the 15.25 port an @cast camera on a bot got no Cast Chat tab. The server wrote the
# open-channel packet (0xAC) at the END of the camera's init message, right behind 0xA7 fight
# modes. 15.25 sends 0xA7 as 3 bytes (TacticsWithoutFightMode); a client whose 15.25 support
# predates that (the installed Redemption build) reads 4, desyncs ("Unhandled opcode 0x00 ...
# previous opcode: 0xA7") and drops the rest of the message, so the tab never opened and every
# STATUS line logged "message in channel id 80 which is unknown". The init now opens the channel
# right after enter-world and sends fight modes as the last packet of the first message.
# The harness client (OTClient 4.2, a correct 1525 parser) proves the channel, the stream and
# the command round trip; the packet order is what makes the older client work too.
# Run: runner.py fix_170_cast_bot_channel.steps --var R=<any bot>   (e.g. Kaelis Duke)
# Acceptance:
#   - the camera gets channel_open for channel 80 "Cast Chat" and game_console holds a tab for it;
#   - at least one STATUS line arrives on channel 80 within 60 s of the login;
#   - `/cavebot "<R>" status` typed into Cast Chat by the camera (@srv cmd via=cam) is echoed on channel 80 and answered (the reply is a status
#     text message, fanned out to the bot's cameras: "[cavebot] Bot '<R>': state=...").
@cam:$R login
@srv expect src=cli:c1 k=channel_open channel=80 name="Cast Chat" min=1 within=60 wait=15
@srv expect src=cli:c1 k=channel_tab channel=80 tab=true min=1 within=60 wait=10
@cam:$R uicheck expect="tabs=\[.*Cast Chat.*\]"
@srv expect src=cli:c1 k=see_talk channel=80 text~="^STATUS: " min=1 within=60 wait=60
@srv cmd "$R" status expect="state=" via=cam
@srv expect src=cli:c1 k=see_talk channel=80 text~="^> /cavebot " min=1 within=20 wait=10
@srv expect src=cli:c1 k=see_msg text~="Bot '$R'.*state=" min=1 within=20 wait=10
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="Lua Script Error" within=120
@cam:$R logout
